.TH FVX 1 "September 2026" "fvx" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fvx \- per-project Flutter SDK switching, no cd hook required
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fvx
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fvx
installs two shims, named \fBflutter\fR and \fBdart\fR, first on PATH. Each shim
runs \fBfvx resolve\fR to find the SDK the current folder pins, then execs the
real binary from that SDK. Because the shims sit on PATH itself, every shell,
script, editor and agent that calls \fBflutter\fR or \fBdart\fR gets the pinned
version automatically. No \fBcd\fR hook is involved.
.PP
A version pin is looked up in this order: the \fBFVX_VERSION\fR environment
variable first; otherwise, walking up from the working directory toward
\fI$HOME\fR, each directory is checked for \fI.fvmrc\fR, then
\fI.fvm/fvm_config.json\fR, then \fI.tool-versions\fR, then the
\fBenvironment.flutter\fR range in \fIpubspec.yaml\fR. The first directory with
an answer wins. When no directory has one, the global default symlink at
\fI~/.flutter-sdk/current\fR is used.
.PP
A pin from \fIpubspec.yaml\fR is a range, not an exact version. The global
default is kept if it satisfies the range; otherwise the highest installed
version that satisfies it is used. An exact pin, or a range that no installed
version satisfies, is an error: \fBfvx\fR never falls back to a different
version silently. It prints what to install and exits non-zero.
.PP
If the \fBfvx\fR binary itself is not on PATH (for example after an
uninstall), the shims exec the global default's binary directly, so
\fBflutter\fR keeps working, just without project pins.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B fvx setup \fR[\fB\-\-print\fR|\fB\-\-uninstall\fR]
Write the \fBflutter\fR and \fBdart\fR shims to \fI~/.fvx/shims\fR and add the
PATH line that puts them first, to \fI~/.zshrc\fR, \fI~/.bashrc\fR and the
fish config, whichever already exist (or the file for \fB$SHELL\fR if none
do). \fB\-\-print\fR shows the PATH line for each shell without writing
anything. \fB\-\-uninstall\fR removes the shims and the PATH block. Also
prints the VS Code / Cursor setting to add once:
\fB"dart.getFlutterSdkCommand": { "executable": "fvx", "args": ["resolve"] }\fR.
.TP
.B fvx use \fR[\fIversion\fR]
Pin the current directory to \fIversion\fR by writing or updating
\fI.fvmrc\fR there. Without a version, an interactive picker lists installed
SDKs, using \fBfzf\fR when it is available. Warns if \fIversion\fR is not
installed yet.
.TP
.B fvx default \fR[\fIversion\fR]
Set the global default SDK, used by any folder with no pin of its own.
Without a version, an interactive picker is shown.
.TP
.B fvx current
Show the version the current folder resolves to, and why: a pin file, or the
global default.
.TP
.B fvx which
Print the path to the real \fBflutter\fR binary the current folder resolves
to.
.TP
.B fvx ls\fR (or \fBlist\fR) [\fB\-\-labels\fR]
List installed SDKs, marking the global default and the one the current
folder resolves to, and flagging any SDK folder whose name no longer matches
the Flutter version inside it. \fB\-\-labels\fR prints one label per line, for
scripting and shell completion.
.TP
.B fvx install \fR[\fIversion\fR]
Download an official Flutter SDK into \fI~/.flutter-sdk\fR, verifying it
against Google's published checksum for the release. Without a version,
installs the exact version pinned by the current folder, if there is one.
The first SDK installed on a machine becomes the default automatically.
.TP
.B fvx rm \fIversion\fR \fR[\fB\-\-yes\fR] (alias: \fBremove\fR)
Delete an installed SDK. Refuses to remove the current global default.
Asks for confirmation on a terminal; scripts must pass \fB\-\-yes\fR.
.TP
.B fvx doctor
Check the setup: the shims are written and current, they come first on PATH,
a global default is set, the current folder resolves, and installed SDK
folder names still match the Flutter version inside them. Exits non-zero if
any check fails.
.TP
.B fvx upgrade \fR[\fB\-\-check\fR]
Check GitHub for a newer \fBfvx\fR release and run the matching upgrade
command for however it was installed (Homebrew, or npm/bun), or print the
release URL for a plain binary install. \fB\-\-check\fR only reports whether
an update is available, without running anything.
.TP
.B fvx completions \fIzsh\fR|\fIbash\fR|\fIfish\fR (alias: \fBcompletion\fR)
Print a shell completion script for the given shell.
.TP
.B fvx resolve
Print the SDK root the current folder resolves to, or exit non-zero with an
explanation. This is what the shims call on every \fBflutter\fR and
\fBdart\fR invocation; it does no network or process work.
.TP
.B fvx version \fR(or \fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR)
Print the \fBfvx\fR version.
.TP
.B fvx help \fR(or \fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR)
Show the command reference. Also shown when no command is given.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FVX_VERSION
Use this version in the current shell, overriding any pin file. Checked
before any directory is walked.
.TP
.B FLUTTER_SDK_HOME
Where SDKs are installed and looked up. Default: \fI~/.flutter-sdk\fR.
.TP
.B FVX_HOME
Relocate everything \fBfvx\fR touches, including the SDK folder, the global
default symlink, the shims, and where the pin walk stops climbing toward
\fI$HOME\fR, under this directory. A fully isolated sandbox, useful for
testing.
.TP
.B FLUTTER_STORAGE_BASE_URL
Mirror to download SDKs from instead of Google's storage, honored by
\fBfvx install\fR the same way the Flutter tool itself honors it.
.TP
.B FVX_DEBUG
Print the full stack trace on an unexpected error, instead of one clean
line.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.flutter-sdk/<label>/flutter
Root of one installed SDK. \fIlabel\fR is usually the version number, but can
be anything.
.TP
.I ~/.flutter-sdk/current
Symlink to the global default SDK.
.TP
.I ~/.fvx/shims/flutter
.TP
.I ~/.fvx/shims/dart
The shims placed first on PATH by \fBfvx setup\fR.
.TP
.I .fvmrc
Per-project pin written by \fBfvx use\fR, and the first file checked when
resolving a folder.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Pin a project, install its SDK, and confirm it resolves:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cd ~/Code/app
fvx use 3.22.3
fvx install 3.22.3
fvx current
.fi
.RE
.PP
Enable the shims once per machine:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fvx setup
exec zsh
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error: an unresolved pin, a missing SDK, a failed \fBdoctor\fR check, or
similar.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled at an interactive prompt (a picker or a delete confirmation).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flutter (1),
.B fvm
.PP
